<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Crash (255)</h1>
<p>Usage:
</p>
<pre>crash the entire game...
</pre>
<p>Crashes the game on purpose, to test what happens when it goes down (the 
core dump, the restart scripts). You must type the whole phrase exactly, 
with the three dots, and the command itself in full: an abbreviation is 
refused. You must be standing. It is logged.
</p><p>It aborts the server, as a failed assertion would, in any build: the 
core dump and the restart follow as after a real crash.
</p><p><i>From the old help:</i> "This wiz-command is the only possible way of 
crashing the game." Kira added: "Maaaybe I'm wrong, but I think there 
might be one or two other ways to crash the game *grin*."
</p><p><br />
See Also:
</p>
<pre>&gt; <a cmd='#'>Wizhelp Reboot</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Wizhelp Shutdown</a>
</pre>




</div>